.TH QPUTRY 1
.SH NAME
qputry \- run a candidate QPU program and report what the firmware did
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qputry
[
.B -c
.I ctlidx
] [
.B -n
.I w0
] [
.B -t
.I w2
] [
.B -x
.I w3
] [
.B -f
]
.I word ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Qputry
writes
.I word
\&... into
.BR /dev/v3dcode ,
enables the QPUs, asks
.B /dev/v3dctl
to run them and prints the device's status. See
.IR v3d (3);
.B "bind -a '#Q' /dev"
first.
.PP
Words are 32-bit, written little-endian in the order given. Nothing
here knows what a QPU instruction looks like \- that is what is being
found out.
.PP
The options set the four words of the
.B EXECUTE_QPU
request and
.B -c
says which of them carries the control list's address. They are
.B not
named after what they do, because what they do is unknown: the layout
.RB ( num_qpus ,
.IR control ,
.IR noflush ,
.IR timeout_ms )
was a guess and the timeout half of it was falsified by a sweep that
moved nothing.
.SH EXAMPLE
Four runs that between them say which word matters:
.IP
.EX
qputry 0xdeadbeef 0xcafebabe        # the believed layout
qputry \-c 0 0xdeadbeef 0xcafebabe   # control address in word 0
qputry \-n 4 0xdeadbeef 0xcafebabe   # vary word 0
qputry \-x 1 0xdeadbeef 0xcafebabe   # vary word 3
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/qputry.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR v3d (3),
.IR draw3dkerntest (1)
.SH BUGS
.B "Read the tag word before anything else."
.IR V3d (3)'s
status prints
.B "tag ... wrote N bytes" ;
if that is
.B UNTOUCHED
or
.BR "wrote 0 bytes" ,
.B EXECUTE_QPU
did nothing and the elapsed time is the cost of a rejected request
rather than of a program running. An earlier version of the device
reported a
.B resp
word that was this program's own
.I w0
coming back, and every figure published through it had to be withdrawn.
.PP
.B "Elapsed time is the signal, not the response code."
A mailbox that accepts the tag and does nothing and a firmware that
runs a program both report success.
.PP
It cannot assemble anything and there is no QPU assembler here: the
instruction encoding is not documented on this machine, so a program
has to be given as words and the encoding established from the
hardware's behaviour.
.PP
.B /dev/v3dcode
appends, so two runs without a
.B reset
concatenate.
.I Qputry
resets first; writing the file by hand does not.
.PP
The word parser rejects anything that is not hex or decimal, which is
load-bearing on a serial console: a dropped character turned
.B 0xcafebabe
into
.B 0xcafexbabe
and the parser refused it rather than running a corrupted program.
